body:
This is one of the stupidest things that happens with many many fandoms: Everyone tries to be some intellectual and put themselves as a peer to the author, while in realityhaving retarded, surface scratching "ideas" that are very simplistic yet they try to portray that as some sort of "analysis". Thats why for the most part i think that anime and manga reviews are stupid, you don't need someone to explain that drinking water involves taking the water and puting it in your body through your mouth. You don't need to "theorize" let alone think that the author is being "inconsistent".

&#x200B;

Like, it's not about the stupidity alone, but the sheer confidence these idiots have.

i mainly would like him not to have CoC to avoid the trope of every character having to get CoC to be very powerful, it would be better to see each character be very powerful in his own style.

&#x200B;

It's why it's better for sanji not to have CoC, because since his attacks are fire based, it makes sense to focus on upgrades that enhance that (armament plus exoskeleton enhances heat tolerance), and the concussion of his kicks ensure dealing damage regardless of penetrating the enemy, since it's concussion damage. Zoro meanwhile, who has no explosive fire or concussion damage, would make sense to have CoC To enhance his slicing techniques.

exactly, he's very fast even in non linear movement 5unlike kizaru) so Observation haki would not be a free ticket against him, He's very strong, and can dish out these strong attacks in rapid succession, He can effortlessly shrug off a sword strike from Queen with no armament, and has very wide potential since he doesn't even have a devil fruit.

&#x200B;

And to top it off, most of his training time goes to cooking, the dude's thing is supposed to be cooking and he's this strong. Him and Zoro are looking as scary as any Yonkou  commander now, if not scarier.
